# Tauri updater signing keys.
#
# The most dangerous file this repo could ever contain. Anyone holding the
# private key can sign an update that every installed copy will trust and
# install without asking — it is a remote code execution primitive on every
# customer's machine, not just a credential. Generate it outside the repo
# (`~/.tauri/`) and keep the only copy in the TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY secret;
# these patterns are the second line of defence, not the first.
*.key
!*.key.example
updater.key*
tauri-updater.key*
.tauri/

